# A PR touching src/execution/ or src/policy/ must reference or add an ADR
# under specs/decisions/ -- mechanically enforced by the `adr-governance`
# check (scripts/adr-governance/check.ts, GOVERNED_PATH_PREFIXES). See
# specs/decisions/ for the reasoning behind past changes to that boundary and
# CONTRIBUTING.md for the contributor-facing summary.
#
# One owner, every path -- no per-directory rules to add here today. The
# review responsibilities that owner exercises (beyond what `npm run
# contract` already verifies mechanically) are in CODE_REVIEW.md, not
# encoded as ownership structure, since a single-owner CODEOWNERS file has
# no scoping left to express: `*` already requires this owner's review on
# every file security-sensitive or not. If a second owner is ever added,
# revisit this file for genuine path-scoped ownership (security
# enforcement, contract orchestration, presets, CI, package/public API
# configuration -- see CODE_REVIEW.md's high-risk change indicators) rather
# than defaulting back to a blanket rule.

